# Valgrind memcheck suppressions for the `valgrind` docker CI leg.
#
# Only for reports that are not ours to fix: allocations the OpenMP, BLAS and
# CUDA-less GPU shim runtimes make once and never free, and known-benign
# reads inside those libraries. Anything in einsums code belongs in a fix, not
# here.
#
# The leg already passes --errors-for-leak-kinds=definite, so still-reachable
# pools (libgomp's thread arenas, OpenBLAS's per-thread buffers) do not need
# suppressing - they are reported but do not fail a test.
#
# To add an entry, re-run the offending test with --gen-suppressions=all and
# paste the generated block, then replace the innermost frames with `...` so
# the rule survives a library update:
#
#   ./devtools/docker/run-ci-leg.sh valgrind -- -R "TheTest" \
#       --overwrite MemoryCheckCommandOptions="--gen-suppressions=all"
#
# Keep each entry commented with what it is and why it is not our bug.

# Example of the intended shape; harmless as written because no such object
# exists. Replace it with a real entry rather than adding alongside it.
#
# {
#    libgomp-thread-pool-teardown
#    Memcheck:Leak
#    match-leak-kinds: possible
#    ...
#    obj:*/libgomp.so*
# }
